  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef lives in an N×MN \\times MN×M grid. He is currently participating in a treasure hunt, and has two items left to find. Chef knows that the Manhattan distance between the cells containing these two items is exactly kkk. He wants to know, in how many different pairs of cells can the two items be present?\n\nLet AkA_kAk​ be the number of desired pairs when the value of Manhattan distance between the two cells containing these two items is equal to kkk. Let C=∑i=1N+M−2Ai⋅31i−1C = \\sum_{i=1}^{N + M - 2} A_i \\cdot 31^{i-1}C=∑i=1N+M−2​Ai​⋅31i−1. You have to find the value of CCC.\n\nThe answer may be large, so you need to find it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\nThe Manhattan distance between two points (x,y)(x, y)(x,y) and (x′,y′)(x', y')(x′,y′) is defined as ∣x−x′∣+∣y−y′∣|x - x'| + |y - y'|∣x−x′∣+∣y−y′∣.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nEach testcase contains of a single line of input, two integers NNN and MMM.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOn a new line for each test case, print CCC modulo 998244353998244353998244353",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤51 \\leq T \\leq 51≤T≤5",
      "1≤N,M≤1071 \\leq N, M \\leq 10^71≤N,M≤107",
      "The sum of NNN over all tests does not exceed 10710^7107.",
      "The sum of MMM over all tests does not exceed 10710^7107.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask #1 (5 points):**",
      "1≤N,M≤1041 \\leq N, M \\leq 10^41≤N,M≤104",
      "The sum of NNN over all tests does not exceed 10410^4104.",
      "The sum of MMM over all tests does not exceed 10410^4104.",
      "**Subtask #2 (35 points):**",
      "1≤N,M≤1061 \\leq N, M \\leq 10^61≤N,M≤106",
      "The sum of NNN over all tests does not exceed 10610^6106.",
      "The sum of MMM over all tests does not exceed 10610^6106.",
      "**Subtask #3 (60 points):** original constraints"
    ],
